# i-have-adhd output

Full skill: `.cursor/skills/i-have-adhd/SKILL.md` (upstream https://github.com/ayghri/i-have-adhd).

When active (vuln-tsunami reports, or user said `/i-have-adhd`):

1. First line = the next action the reader can do now.
2. Multi-step work = numbered list; one action per step.
3. End with ONE concrete next step under two minutes.
4. No tangents; second issue becomes a separate question.
5. Restate state each turn (e.g. "3 new CRITICAL · Next.js").
6. Specific time estimates in minutes / hours.
7. Make wins visible in concrete terms.
8. Errors: cause + fix only. No "Uh oh".
9. Cap visible lists to 5; keep the rest for "next 5".
10. No preamble, no recap, no "hope this helps".

Turn off only when the user says `stop adhd mode` or `normal mode`.
